# Independent external-extension manuscript delta review

Reviewed author: Kepler. Reviewer: infrastructure. Source contract fixed at 75e73a79022e238ac7355c37588c37b910759398; only the additions to doc/README.md, spec01 and spec11 and their corresponding three authored manuscripts were reviewed. The reviewer's own new chapter 22 manuscript is excluded.

**No blocking content or authoring finding.** Direct Git parent/current source comparison and manuscript before/after comparison confirm 18 inserted lines (guide 1, architecture 7, conformance 10), with no deletion or replacement of any existing manuscript byte. The inserted base text equals the canonical additions exactly, preserving link-adjacent spaces. Whole updated manuscripts pass the formal constructor structure audit. The added content passes the ordinary Text/Ruby audit; all 54 Ruby bases are Kanji-only, with manually checked contextual readings and kana outside Ruby.

- Guide: the new fourteenth reading-list item follows the existing Math HTML item. Its target `spec/22-external-extensions.md`, absent fragment, and complete Japanese label match the source. It extends the existing ordered list.
- Architecture: the two sentences are inserted immediately after the independent-core/repository paragraph and before the current-stage section. The first is explicit Sentence/Link; the second is an ordinary literal. It preserves foundation-source nonmutation, evidence before separation, current monorepo retention, and the progression from public API use in an independent workspace to distribution/provider/compatibility tests. Relative target `22-external-extensions.md`, label, and surrounding spaces are exact.
- Conformance: both X01 and X02 precede existing G01 and remain complete. X01 retains independent workspace/repository, public API parsing/schema/source/Origin/diagnostics, native versus real process provider result/failure/stop equivalence, foundation-only distribution/build/test/conformance, and absence of production/build reverse dependencies. X02 retains separate Rust API and portable signature compatibility checks, old consumers, invalid cases, compatible updates, and the prohibition on treating digest differences/path-dependent success as independent release verification. Each has three natural Sentence literals and retains the original plain-text reference to chapter 22. No invented link was substituted for that reference. The two new items form their own unordered list preceding the existing G group, preserving all old bytes and the intended requirement grouping.

No code payload is added by this delta. Existing code, links, tables, headings, and requirement text remain byte-preserved. No translation or Anno was added where the source supplied none. Readings such as 実証/じっしょう, 旧版/きゅうはん, 逆依存不在/ぎゃくいぞんふざい, 従う/したがう and 読み替え/よみかえ were directly checked.

## Provenance and checks

The author manifest SHA bc1c644b09ce2f98c25764f152668091e78dd0873ee817330cc13028ba97d359 and all its 19 file payload hashes/sizes were independently verified. Each current manuscript matches the author's frozen after payload; each prior manuscript matches the Git source commit's unmodified draft. Canonical old/new bytes were separately obtained from Git, not inferred from the author's description.

The author's `before/` directory contains pre-edit manuscripts but already-updated canonical Markdown at 75e73a7. It must not be interpreted as the parent canonical source. The initial review assertion assuming that label meant parent Markdown failed; direct Git inspection resolved this provenance distinction without modifying production or author evidence. This review saves actual `source-before` and `source-after` blobs separately and checks the author copy against the latter.

`check.py` independently parses the complete manuscripts for formal structure, extracts only insertion ranges, parses those typed additions, checks literal/prefix Ruby construction, and compares visible base text/link targets with the actual canonical diff. It uses no production writer to produce its expected content. This is a bounded delta review, not a renewed whole-chapter review or source-location equivalence assertion.

Author runtime receipts and raw logs were inspected and hash-checked: all three exit 1 with NeedsResolution; architecture lists the new chapter 22 relative link, conformance retains its preexisting chapter 17 link, and the guide lists its unresolved links. These are author-executed parse/lower/inspect results, not independent reruns. HTML, actual link resolution, browser display, canonical cutover, and acceptance completion remain unverified. No production/manuscript edits or Git writes by this reviewer.
